# Opinion

Meeting: 0020-ensure-docker-deployment-uses-real-auth-for-web-client
Agent: NoteTaker
Task: ensure docker deployment uses real auth for web client
Context:
- Web client needed to stop showing seed data in prod and instead require real API + OIDC with secure crypto.
- Docker builds also needed a runtime-config bridge for issuer/client details.
Position:
- Team aligned on enforcing HTTPS + JWKS for any remote sync and failing fast when `apiBaseUrl` or OIDC inputs are missing.
- Runtime entrypoint now writes `runtime-config.js` from env vars; app.js blocks until tokens are present and verified.
Recommendations:
- Validate `/state` contract against the live backend and schedule a smoke that exercises JWKS fetch + auth redirect to prevent regressions.
- Capture auth failure telemetry in the client to speed debugging when issuer or config drift occurs post-deploy.
